WEBVTT

00:00:04.961 --> 00:00:07.094
[♪♪♪]

00:01:08.720 --> 00:01:11.723
[RATTLING AND SQUEALING]

00:01:11.723 --> 00:01:13.334
I can't let you out, Hedwig.

00:01:13.334 --> 00:01:15.727
I'm not allowed
to use magic outside of school.

00:01:17.990 --> 00:01:19.383
Besides, if Uncle Vernon--

00:01:19.383 --> 00:01:22.256
UNCLE VERNON:
Harry Potter!

00:01:22.256 --> 00:01:24.823
Now you've done it.

00:01:24.823 --> 00:01:26.564
[HUMMING]

00:01:29.393 --> 00:01:31.091
He's in there.
Vernon...

00:01:33.789 --> 00:01:35.269
I'm warning you.

00:01:35.269 --> 00:01:36.879
If you can't control
that bloody bird,

00:01:36.879 --> 00:01:38.446
it'll have to go.

00:01:38.446 --> 00:01:40.448
But she's bored.

00:01:40.448 --> 00:01:43.407
If I could only
let her out for...

00:01:43.407 --> 00:01:45.148
an hour or two.

00:01:45.148 --> 00:01:47.629
So you can send secret messages
to your freaky little friends?

00:01:47.629 --> 00:01:48.804
No, sir.

00:01:48.804 --> 00:01:50.501
But I haven't had
any messages.

00:01:50.501 --> 00:01:53.156
From any of my friends.

00:01:53.156 --> 00:01:55.419
Not one.

00:01:56.768 --> 00:01:58.205
All summer.

00:01:58.205 --> 00:02:01.382
Who would want to be friends
with you?

00:02:03.949 --> 00:02:05.951
I should think
you'd be a little more grateful.

00:02:05.951 --> 00:02:07.997
We've raised you
since you were a baby,

00:02:07.997 --> 00:02:09.955
given you the food
off our table,

00:02:09.955 --> 00:02:12.306
even let you have
Dudley's second bedroom,

00:02:12.306 --> 00:02:15.047
purely out of the goodness
of our hearts.

00:02:15.047 --> 00:02:17.702
Not now, bobkins.
It's for when the Masons arrive.

00:02:17.702 --> 00:02:21.706
Which should be any minute.

00:02:21.706 --> 00:02:23.969
Now, let's go over our schedule
once again, shall we?

00:02:23.969 --> 00:02:26.668
Petunia, when the Masons arrive,
you will be...?

00:02:26.668 --> 00:02:28.278
In the lounge,

00:02:28.278 --> 00:02:30.672
waiting to welcome them
graciously to our home.

00:02:30.672 --> 00:02:31.977
Good. And, Dudley,

00:02:31.977 --> 00:02:33.240
you will be...?

00:02:33.240 --> 00:02:34.763
I'll be waiting
to open the door.

00:02:34.763 --> 00:02:37.287
Excellent.

00:02:41.335 --> 00:02:43.250
And you?

00:02:43.250 --> 00:02:44.512
I'll be in my bedroom,

00:02:44.512 --> 00:02:46.340
making no noise

00:02:46.340 --> 00:02:48.168
and pretending
that I don't exist.

00:02:48.168 --> 00:02:49.560
Too right, you will.

00:02:49.560 --> 00:02:50.605
With any luck,

00:02:50.605 --> 00:02:52.433
this could well be the day

00:02:52.433 --> 00:02:54.696
I make the biggest deal
of my career,

00:02:54.696 --> 00:02:57.438
and you will not mess it up.

00:02:58.917 --> 00:03:00.702
[DOORBELL RINGS]

00:03:00.702 --> 00:03:02.747
Mr. and Mrs. Mason,
welcome...

00:03:02.747 --> 00:03:05.402
[LAUGHING]

00:03:08.362 --> 00:03:10.581
Harry Potter...

00:03:10.581 --> 00:03:13.410
such an honor it is.

00:03:16.108 --> 00:03:17.327
Who are you?

00:03:17.327 --> 00:03:21.201
Dobby, sir.
Dobby the house-elf.

00:03:21.201 --> 00:03:23.072
Not to be rude or anything,

00:03:23.072 --> 00:03:24.813
but this isn't
a great time for me

00:03:24.813 --> 00:03:26.989
to have a house-elf
in my bedroom.

00:03:26.989 --> 00:03:29.600
Yes, sir, Dobby understands.

00:03:29.600 --> 00:03:33.038
It's just that Dobby
has come to tell you...

00:03:33.038 --> 00:03:35.998
It is difficult, sir.

00:03:35.998 --> 00:03:37.869
Dobby wonders
where to begin.

00:03:37.869 --> 00:03:39.480
Why don't you sit down?

00:03:39.480 --> 00:03:41.960
S-sit down?

00:03:41.960 --> 00:03:44.572
Sit down?

00:03:44.572 --> 00:03:47.618
[SOBBING]

00:03:47.618 --> 00:03:49.577
Dobby, shush. I'm sorry.

00:03:49.577 --> 00:03:51.709
I didn't mean
to offend you or anything.

00:03:51.709 --> 00:03:53.189
Offend Dobby?

00:03:54.495 --> 00:03:56.975
Dobby has heard
of your greatness, sir,

00:03:56.975 --> 00:04:00.805
but never has he been asked
to sit down by a wizard...

00:04:00.805 --> 00:04:02.938
like an equal.

00:04:02.938 --> 00:04:06.507
You can't have met
many decent wizards, then.

00:04:06.507 --> 00:04:08.857
No, I haven't.

00:04:08.857 --> 00:04:10.815
That was an awful thing to say.

00:04:12.426 --> 00:04:13.601
Bad Dobby!

00:04:13.601 --> 00:04:14.993
Stop, Dobby!

00:04:14.993 --> 00:04:16.038
Dobby, please!

00:04:16.038 --> 00:04:17.561
Dobby, please, stop.

00:04:19.302 --> 00:04:21.478
[BANGING]

00:04:21.478 --> 00:04:24.699
Don't mind that.
It's just the cat.

00:04:26.570 --> 00:04:27.702
Stop!

00:04:27.702 --> 00:04:29.225
Bad Dobby!
Stop, Dobby!

00:04:29.225 --> 00:04:31.314
Please, be quiet.

00:04:31.314 --> 00:04:34.491
Are you all right?

00:04:34.491 --> 00:04:37.015
Dobby had to
punish himself, sir.

00:04:37.015 --> 00:04:40.280
Dobby almost spoke ill
of his family, sir.

00:04:40.280 --> 00:04:42.064
Your family?

00:04:42.064 --> 00:04:44.327
The wizard family
Dobby serves, sir.

00:04:44.327 --> 00:04:47.765
Dobby is bound to serve
one family forever.

00:04:47.765 --> 00:04:50.725
If they ever knew
Dobby was here...

00:04:50.725 --> 00:04:52.857
Ooh!

00:04:52.857 --> 00:04:54.250
But Dobby had to come.

00:04:54.250 --> 00:04:58.167
Dobby has to protect
Harry Potter. To warn him.

00:04:58.167 --> 00:05:00.169
Harry Potter must not go back

00:05:00.169 --> 00:05:03.128
to Hogwarts School
of Witchcraft and Wizardry

00:05:03.128 --> 00:05:04.260
this year.

00:05:04.260 --> 00:05:06.784
There is a plot.

00:05:06.784 --> 00:05:10.832
A plot to make
most terrible things happen.

00:05:10.832 --> 00:05:13.487
What terrible things?
Who's plotting them?

00:05:13.487 --> 00:05:14.662
Oh, he...

00:05:14.662 --> 00:05:16.054
can't...

00:05:16.054 --> 00:05:17.665
say!

00:05:17.665 --> 00:05:21.321
Okay, I understand.
You can't say.

00:05:24.846 --> 00:05:26.587
Dobby!

00:05:26.587 --> 00:05:28.545
Dobby,
put the lamp down.

00:05:28.545 --> 00:05:31.331
So, when they arrive
at the ninth hole...

00:05:31.331 --> 00:05:35.160
[BANGING AND GROANING]

00:05:35.160 --> 00:05:37.032
Give me the lamp!

00:05:38.816 --> 00:05:41.384
Dobby, stop!

00:05:44.605 --> 00:05:46.955
Get in there and keep quiet!

00:05:46.955 --> 00:05:49.523
What the devil
are you doing up here?

00:05:49.523 --> 00:05:51.786
I was just--

00:05:51.786 --> 00:05:54.354
You just ruined the punchline
of my Japanese-golfer joke.

00:05:54.354 --> 00:05:56.312
Sorry.

00:05:57.879 --> 00:05:59.315
One more sound,

00:05:59.315 --> 00:06:01.839
and you'll wish
you'd never been born, boy.

00:06:01.839 --> 00:06:02.927
And fix that door.

00:06:02.927 --> 00:06:04.799
Yes, sir.

00:06:07.889 --> 00:06:09.586
See why
I've got to go back?

00:06:09.586 --> 00:06:11.066
I don't belong here.

00:06:11.066 --> 00:06:13.329
I belong in your world,
at Hogwarts.

00:06:13.329 --> 00:06:15.766
It's the only place
I've got friends.

00:06:15.766 --> 00:06:18.639
Friends who don't even write
to Harry Potter?

00:06:18.639 --> 00:06:20.380
Well, I expect they've been...

00:06:20.380 --> 00:06:22.425
Hang on.

00:06:22.425 --> 00:06:25.123
How do you know my friends
haven't been writing to me?

00:06:27.082 --> 00:06:29.389
Harry Potter
mustn't be angry with Dobby.

00:06:29.389 --> 00:06:31.086
Dobby hoped

00:06:31.086 --> 00:06:34.306
if Harry Potter thought
his friends had forgotten him,

00:06:34.306 --> 00:06:38.267
Harry Potter might not want
to go back to school, sir.

00:06:38.267 --> 00:06:41.836
Give me those...now.

00:06:41.836 --> 00:06:44.839
No!

00:06:55.937 --> 00:06:58.853
Dobby, get back here.

00:07:02.160 --> 00:07:04.336
Dobby...

00:07:04.336 --> 00:07:05.990
Please, no.

00:07:05.990 --> 00:07:10.386
Harry Potter must say
he's not going back to school.

00:07:10.386 --> 00:07:13.171
I can't.
Hogwarts is my home.

00:07:13.171 --> 00:07:19.351
Then Dobby must do it, sir,
for Harry Potter's own good.

00:07:23.834 --> 00:07:26.010
...one plumber said,
"Look at all that water,"

00:07:26.010 --> 00:07:28.360
and the second plumber said,
"Yes...

00:07:28.360 --> 00:07:31.233
and that's
just the top of it."

00:07:40.938 --> 00:07:42.810
I'm so sorry.

00:07:42.810 --> 00:07:45.552
It's my nephew.
He's very disturbed.

00:07:45.552 --> 00:07:47.510
Meeting strangers
upsets him.

00:07:47.510 --> 00:07:49.991
That's why
I kept him upstairs.

00:07:55.953 --> 00:07:57.172
[DRILL WHIRRING]

00:08:01.655 --> 00:08:04.222
You're never going
back to that school.

00:08:04.222 --> 00:08:05.397
You're never
going to see

00:08:05.397 --> 00:08:07.356
those freaky friends
of yours again.

00:08:07.356 --> 00:08:08.836
Never!

00:08:12.013 --> 00:08:15.016
[♪♪♪]

00:08:21.544 --> 00:08:24.504
[ENGINE RATTLING]

